@page
@model BeeMemoryBank.Web.Pages.Admin.SnapshotsModel

@section About {
    <p>
        A <strong>snapshot</strong> is a complete copy of this node at one moment: its database (articles, folders, tags, comments, versions, users, key slots, the
        node's identity, the trusted nodes) and its encrypted files, packed into one file and encrypted under the master key. Snapshots are your backups. Make one
        before anything risky: an update, a restore, a key rotation. You can copy the files out of the data folder whenever you like, even while the node runs, and
        a file can only be opened by someone who has the master password.
    </p>
    <p>
        From this page you can <strong>create</strong> a snapshot, <strong>download</strong> one to keep elsewhere, <strong>upload</strong> one made by this vault (on
        this node, or on another node of the same network) and <strong>delete</strong> one you no longer need. <strong>Restore</strong> opens a dialog with two
        choices, and they are very different:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>This node only</strong> replaces everything on this node with the snapshot. The node becomes a <em>new</em> node: new identity, and it forgets the nodes it
            trusted, its blind copies and its sync history, so the other devices have to be joined to it again. The server is unavailable while it restores, and you sign in afterwards.</li>
        <li><strong>The whole network</strong> asks every trusted node to restore the same snapshot. This node keeps its identity; each other node applies it when it next
            syncs, and only if it trusts this node as a superadmin and has Auto-restore switched on for it (<a href="/Admin/TrustedNodes">Trusted Nodes</a>).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Both ask for the master password. A restore of the whole network always takes a safety backup of this node first; for this node only, the box
        &ldquo;Create backup before restore&rdquo; is ticked for you. A restore replaces content: it cannot be undone except from another snapshot.
        <a href="https://github.com/ultrathinker/BeeMemoryBank/blob/main/docs/snapshot-restore.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">What a restore does</a>.
    </p>
}

@* The upload, the restore and the network restore are sent by admin.js with this token (no form of the page may be there to carry one: an empty list has none). *@
@Html.AntiForgeryToken()

<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:flex-end;margin-bottom:12px;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
    <sl-button size="small" variant="default" id="btn-show-upload">
        <sl-icon slot="prefix" name="cloud-upload"></sl-icon> Upload
    </sl-button>
    <sl-button size="small" variant="success" id="btn-create-snapshot">
        <sl-icon slot="prefix" name="plus-lg"></sl-icon> Create Snapshot
    </sl-button>
</div>

<div id="snapshot-upload-zone"
     style="display:none;border:2px dashed var(--text-secondary);padding:20px;text-align:center;border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:16px;cursor:pointer;transition:background 0.15s;">
    <sl-icon name="cloud-upload" style="font-size:1.6rem;color:var(--text-secondary);"></sl-icon>
    <p style="margin:8px 0 4px 0;">
        Drag &amp; drop a snapshot file (<code>.tar.gz</code> / <code>.bin</code>)
        or <sl-button variant="text" id="btn-pick-file">browse</sl-button>
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin:0;">Uploaded snapshots appear in the list below and can be restored.</p>
    <input type="file" id="snapshot-file-input" accept=".tar.gz,.bin" style="display:none;" />
    <div id="upload-progress" style="display:none;margin-top:12px;">
        <sl-progress-bar id="upload-progress-bar" value="0"></sl-progress-bar>
        <span id="upload-status" class="text-sm text-muted"></span>
    </div>
</div>

@if (Model.Snapshots != null && Model.Snapshots.Count > 0)
{
    <div class="card" style="padding:0;overflow:hidden;">
        <table class="version-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>File</th>
                    <th>Size</th>
                    <th>Date</th>
                    <th style="text-align:right;">Actions</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var snap in Model.Snapshots)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><code class="text-sm">@snap.FileName</code></td>
                        <td class="text-muted text-sm">@(snap.SizeBytes / 1024) KB</td>
                        <td class="text-muted text-sm">@snap.CreatedAt.ToString("g")</td>
                        <td style="text-align:right;">
                            <a href="/Admin/Snapshots?handler=DownloadSnapshot&fileName=@Uri.EscapeDataString(snap.FileName)"
                               title="Download snapshot">
                                <sl-icon-button name="download" label="Download"></sl-icon-button>
                            </a>
                            <sl-icon-button name="arrow-counterclockwise" label="Restore"
                                class="btn-open-restore-snapshot"
                                data-filename="@snap.FileName">
                            </sl-icon-button>
                            <form data-busy="short" method="post" asp-page-handler="DeleteSnapshot" style="display:inline;">
                                <input type="hidden" name="fileName" value="@snap.FileName" />
                                <sl-icon-button name="trash" label="Delete"
                                    class="btn-confirm-submit"
                                    data-confirm-pattern="Delete snapshot {name}?"
                                    data-name="@snap.FileName">
                                </sl-icon-button>
                            </form>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
}
else
{
    <div class="card" style="text-align:center;padding:40px;">
        <sl-icon name="archive" style="font-size:2rem;color:var(--text-secondary);display:block;margin-bottom:12px;"></sl-icon>
        <p class="text-muted">No snapshots</p>
    </div>
}

<!-- Restore Snapshot Dialog -->
@{
    var activePeers = (Model.Whitelist ?? new()).Count(w => w.Status == "A");
    var autoRestorePeers = (Model.Whitelist ?? new()).Count(w => w.Status == "A" && w.AutoAcceptRestore);
}
<sl-dialog id="dlg-restore-snapshot" label="Restore Snapshot" style="--width: 640px;">
    <input type="hidden" name="fileName" id="restore-file-name" />
    <p style="margin-top:0;">Snapshot: <code id="restore-snapshot-name-display"></code></p>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm">A snapshot can be restored here only when it was made by this vault: this node, or another node in the same network that shares its master key. A snapshot from a different vault cannot be opened here, whichever password is entered.</p>

    <sl-radio-group id="restore-mode" name="restoreMode" label="What should be restored?" value="standalone" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <sl-radio value="standalone">Restore this node only <span class="text-muted">(it leaves the network and becomes a new node)</span></sl-radio>
        <sl-radio value="network">Restore the whole network from this snapshot</sl-radio>
    </sl-radio-group>

    <div id="restore-mode-standalone">
        <sl-alert variant="danger" open style="margin-bottom:16px;">
            <sl-icon slot="icon" name="exclamation-triangle"></sl-icon>
            <strong>This node becomes a new node.</strong> Everything on this node is replaced with the snapshot, and:
            <ul style="margin:8px 0 0 20px;">
                <li>It gets a <strong>new identity</strong>: a new node id and a new signing key (the name stays).</li>
                <li>It <strong>forgets</strong> the nodes it trusted (@activePeers now), its <strong>blind copies</strong> (on a PC, a Mac or a phone) and its <strong>sync history</strong>.</li>
                <li>Your other devices still know the old node: <strong>join them to this node again</strong>.</li>
                <li><strong>Pair the blind copies again.</strong></li>
                <li>The server is unavailable while it restores, and you sign in again afterwards.</li>
            </ul>
        </sl-alert>
    </div>

    <div id="restore-mode-network" hidden>
        <sl-alert variant="warning" open style="margin-bottom:16px;">
            <sl-icon slot="icon" name="exclamation-triangle"></sl-icon>
            <strong>Every node of the network is asked to restore this snapshot.</strong>
            <ul style="margin:8px 0 0 20px;">
                <li>This node keeps its identity, its users and the nodes it trusts; its articles, folders, tags and media are replaced with the snapshot's.</li>
                <li>Each other node applies it when it next syncs, and <strong>only if</strong> it trusts this node as a superadmin and has <em>Auto-restore</em> switched on for this node (Admin &rarr; Trusted Nodes). Today @autoRestorePeers of @activePeers trusted node(s) have it on. A node without it does not apply the restore.</li>
                <li>Keep this node running and reachable: the others download the snapshot from it (the offer is open for 30 days).</li>
                <li>Blind copies are reseeded.</li>
                <li>A safety backup of this node is always taken first.</li>
            </ul>
            <div style="margin-top:8px;">Only a superadmin can start it, and the vault must be unlocked.</div>
        </sl-alert>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <sl-input name="masterPassword" id="restore-master-password" label="Master Password" type="password" password-toggle required autocomplete="off"></sl-input>
    </div>
    <div id="restore-backup-row" style="margin-bottom:8px;">
        <sl-checkbox name="createBackupFirst" id="restore-backup-checkbox" checked>Create backup before restore</sl-checkbox>
    </div>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm" style="margin:0;">
        <a href="https://github.com/ultrathinker/BeeMemoryBank/blob/main/docs/snapshot-restore.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">What a restore does</a>
    </p>
    <sl-button type="button" slot="footer" variant="default" data-dlg-cancel="dlg-restore-snapshot">Cancel</sl-button>
    <sl-button type="button" slot="footer" variant="danger" id="btn-restore-confirm">
        <sl-icon slot="prefix" name="arrow-counterclockwise"></sl-icon> Restore
    </sl-button>
</sl-dialog>
